.TH BUFFER_DUMMYREADMMAP 3
.SH NAME
buffer_dummyreadmmap \- dummy read function for memory-mapped buffers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <buffer.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t buffer_dummyreadmmap(fd_type " fd ", void* " buf ", size_t " len ", buffer* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR buffer_dummyreadmmap ()
is a placeholder read callback used for memory-mapped buffers where the
data is already mapped in memory and no further reading is required.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Always returns 0.